\section{The extension: derivations, tests and development results}
\label{app:ext}

\paragraph{AdamW in the aligned basis.}
AdamW updates a coordinate $x$ as $x\leftarrow(1-\eta\lambda)x-\eta\,\hat m/(\sqrt{\hat v}+\epsilon)$; the decay is decoupled and enters neither moment.
With diagonal $\Sigma_c$, $\Sigma_{tc}$, a diagonal initial encoder and $\Pred_0=p_0I$, every off-diagonal entry of $\Wc$ and $\Pred$ has zero gradient, so its moments stay zero and decoupled decay keeps it at zero: the matrix iteration is exactly $n$ scalar AdamW maps with gradients $G_a=-a\gamma(p)$ and $G_p=-a^2(c-p\sigma)$ (index $k$ dropped).
(i)~\emph{Transit.} While a gradient keeps its sign over the window $1/(1-\beta_2)$, the step is close to $\eta\,\mathrm{sign}(G)$, so $|\dot p|\approx\eta$ towards $c/\sigma$ and $\dot a\approx\eta(\mathrm{sign}\,\gamma(p)-\lambda a)$; the sign of $G_a$ is that of $\gamma(p)$, so the window is $0<p<c/\sigma$.
(ii)~\emph{Collapse and re-escape.} Outside the window $a$ oscillates about $0$, its gradient stops feeding $\hat v_a$, and the iteration is heavy-ball descent with frozen preconditioner $s_t$: $a_{t+1}=(1-\eta\lambda)a_t-\eta\hat m_t/s_t$, $m_t=\beta_1m_{t-1}-(1-\beta_1)\gamma a_t$.
With $q=\eta(1-\beta_1)|\gamma|/s$ the per-step factor solves $z^2-(1+\beta_1-q)z+\beta_1=0$; while the roots are complex $|z|=\sqrt{\beta_1}$, whatever the curvature.
Since $s_t$ decays as $\beta_2^{t/2}$ (bias-corrected), a real root crosses $-1$ at $q_t=2(1+\beta_1)$, the stability loss of heavy-ball; meanwhile $p$ moves only by decoupled decay.
The oscillation then grows until it refills $\hat v_a$, at $|a|\approx\eta(1-\beta_1)/(2(1+\beta_1)\sqrt{1-\beta_2})$, and $p$ is captured.
(iii)~\emph{Hover.} After capture below $\theta$, stationarity of $p$ under decoupled decay gives the curvature $a$ sees, and $a$ grows at a log rate that the model integrates in closed form until $|a|$ crosses $\theta$ or $p$ reaches its own edge of stability, after which a short exact segment of the scalar map is run.
(iv)~\emph{Settled state.} Captured, $p$ chatters at its momentum stability limit; both normalised updates carry the same filtered residual $c-p\sigma$, and stationarity of their means under decoupled decay gives $\lambda|a|=\lambda|p|$, with $\bar p=c/\sigma$ to leading order.
On the two development grids the settled $|a_T|$ and $|p_T|$ of captured directions sit at $c/\sigma$ (\texttt{results/e4/dev*/settled\_state.txt}); once $\lambda c/\sigma>1$, which no grid here reaches, the amplitude sits at the box edge $1/\lambda$ instead.
The model of the A1 grid (v3) lacks (iv); v4 adds it and was frozen before grid H2.
At the derived horizon, settling can take two stages in the slowest cell ($|a|$ stalls on a plateau below $c/\sigma$ after $p$ has reached it), which is the late capture that fails A2.
\Cref{fig:ext-a} shows the A2$'$ count against the truth for v4 and the baselines.

